// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - FinalAmbushDefeated 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P884682166" "You've recorded a new hit single with Johnny Sonata, entitled, 'Rule the World'!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3746042497" "Always a professional, {HeroName}. I heard there was quite a ruckus in the Giza from the song Johnny was singing. I can only assume that means that everything went according to plan.<br><br>That means part one is done. Part two, however, is something that... you may not exactly enjoy. It involves a safe house and the sewers in Paragon."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Dirge 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2588668060" "<color orange>You find a crate within the sewers with some equipment in it that will allow you to broadcast the Dirge of Chaos directly into the safe house.<br><br>You put in earplugs to prevent you from hearing the Dirge directly and begin to play the song!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P4047514343" "<color orange>You go through the systems on the computer and sabotage them, stopping any hero from coming in and turning off the Dirge of Chaos. Now, there is only one option left, which is for Sister Psyche to absorb the negative energy!<br><br>However, something on one of the nearby cameras catches your eye...</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2922435636" "(Zoom in on the image)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1338179777" "<color orange>You see Manticore with a squad of PPD, just like Tyrka predicted. Now, you <i>could</i> simply walk away with the belief that Manticore could never stop your plan.<br><br>But that's a rookie mistake. You'll have to go beat the tar out of Manticore to make sure that he can't get anywhere near the computer system to stop this plan!</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2413415078" "Malaise is not being kept in the Zig. It's a smart move on their part; we had stolen detailed plans on the infrastructure of the Zig from Arachnos some time ago.<br><br>No, instead they have Malaise in a safe house nearby, one that is armed to the teeth to ensure no one tries a direct assault. Even you, {HeroName}, would be blasted to bits if you tried to walk in there. To be fair, almost <i>anyone</i> would be blasted to bits if they walked in there.<br><br>Luckily for us, the Dirge of Chaos will allow us to walk right into that safe house. We hook into the speaker system that's within the safe house to play the music, causing everyone to go crazy."
// AcceptString :
"P2366258354" "And then I'll need to ensure that system cannot be turned off."
// SendOffString :
"P3045624666" "Exactly. I have a good feeling that <color yellow>Manticore</color> will be able to figure out how to turn that system off. Now, he may or may not actually be there, but it's imperative that we leave Sister Psyche with no other option than to <i>absorb</i> the negative energy being given off by the music.<br><br>This will put her in an extremely weakened state, allowing Malaise to dive inside of her mind. Now, we've stolen one of the Nemesis mole machines. It will get you to the sewer network below the safe house.<br><br>We're already cutting it close, as the safe house has several precautions to check for any major underground disturbances. This is why you may have quite a trek to get up there. Once you set up the Dirge, the security systems should freak out, allowing you to simply leave the sewers and <i>walk</i> into the front door.<br><br>As you can see, {HeroName}, there is quite a lot riding on this. <color orange>Just be careful, as you'll most likely have to fight off Manticore, if he's there.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1525456298" "Play the Dirge of Chaos"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3483290177" "We risk Malaise being moved to another safe house if we wait too long, {HeroName}."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3723698915" "<color deepskyblue>Part II: The Sound of Chaos</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3964314943" "The Nemesis machine shoots out from the ground, leaving you within the depths of the Paragon sewer system."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - ObjectiveUIText 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ObjectiveUIText :
"P2500569351" "Get to the sewers and set up the dirge within one of the crates"

